Author:     Magnus Melin <mkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi>
AuthorDate: Thu Sep 10 13:20:48 2026 +0300
Commit:     mkmelin@iki.fi <mkmelin@iki.fi>
CommitDate: Thu Sep 10 10:22:02 2026 +0000

    Bug 2070818 - Stop the post-message-load work when the message pane navigates away. r=darktrojan

    onEndMsgDownload runs the phishing detector, notifies MsgMsgDisplayed, rewrites
    in-message anchors and shrinks oversized images once a message has loaded. It is
    called fire-and-forget, and it assumes throughout that the message it started
    with is still in the pane.

    Loading a web page over the message breaks that assumption: the pane switches
    content process, so the message's window global and its MailMessage actor go
    away. Depending on when the switch lands, PhishingDetector.analyzeMessage either
    can't reach the actor at all, or has its AnalyzeMessageBody query aborted
    mid-flight, or the link rewriting runs on a document which no longer exists.

    Anchor the work on the URL of the message which loaded, and bail out at each
    point where the pane may have moved on
    Have analyzeMessage report no phishing rather than throwing when the
    actor is gone, keeping the narrow AbortError catch so real errors from the child
    still propagate.

    Also null-check the docShell in onDOMContentLoaded. The listener that
    onHeadersComplete installs outlives the message load, so it can fire for the web
    page instead of the message.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324887

